   {"on": "let down an iron hand swung on a chain", "text": "The famous 'claw of Archimedes': a crane that hooked a ship's prow, lifted it with a lever, and let it drop. Later writers added that he set the Roman fleet on fire with mirrors; Polybius, the earliest source, says nothing of mirrors, and most historians doubt it."},
